        "body": "For generations, the Indian fashion and beauty industry has operated under a deeply toxic and scientifically baseless hierarchy: the idea that lighter skin is inherently more beautiful, more versatile, and easier to dress. This bias—known as Colorism—has not only caused immeasurable psychological damage but has also resulted in objectively terrible fashion advice for millions of Indians. The obsessive cultural preference for fairness has led stylists, influencers, and family members to give deeply flawed, biologically inaccurate color recommendations to anyone who isn't \"fair.\" It is time to dismantle this toxic framework using optical physics."
